title: $:/changenotes/5.5.0/#9981/impacts/two-digit-year
changenote: $:/changenotes/5.5.0/#9981
tags: $:/tags/ImpactNote
impact-type: compatibility-break
description: The `YY` and `wYY` date format tokens now show the last two digits of the year, so years outside 2000 to 2099 render differently.

Up to 5.4.1 `YY` and `wYY` subtracted 2000 from the year rather than taking its last two digits. Within 2000 to 2099 the two are the same, which is why this went unnoticed.

Outside that range the old result was not a two digit year at all:

|!Year |!Up to 5.4.1 |!From 5.5.0 |
|1999 |`-1` |`99` |
|2100 |`100` |`00` |
|-2014 |`-4014` |`14` |

Anything that stored or matched the old output for a year before 2000 or after 2099 needs updating. Use `YYYY` where the full year is wanted, or `aYYYY` to show a negative year as positive.
